     "execution_count": 1,
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "execute_result"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "for _, row in launch_sites_df.iterrows():\n",
    "    coordinate = [row['Lat'], row['Long']]\n",
    "    circle = folium.Circle(\n",
    "        coordinate, radius=1000, color='#d35400', fill=True\n",
    "    ).add_child(folium.Popup(row['Launch Site']))\n",
    "    marker = folium.map.Marker(\n",
    "        coordinate,\n",
    "        icon=DivIcon(\n",
    "            icon_size=(20, 20),\n",
    "            icon_anchor=(0, 0),\n",
    "            html='<div style=\"font-size: 12; color:#d35400;\"><b>%s</b></div>' % row['Launch Site'],\n",
    "        )\n",
    "    )\n",
    "    site_map.add_child(circle)\n",
    "    site_map.add_child(marker)\n",
    "\n",
    "site_map"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "4716926a",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "All four launch sites are close to the coast (for safety, so a failed rocket falls into the\n",
    "ocean rather than over land) and all sit at fairly low latitudes, close to the Equator, which\n",
    "gives rockets an extra eastward velocity boost from Earth's rotation."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "e0ed31e9",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## TASK 2: Mark the success/failed launches for each site on the map"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 1,
   "id": "14c70c27",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "text/plain": [
       "     Launch Site        Lat       Long  class\n",
       "46    KSC LC-39A  28.573255 -80.646895      1\n",
       "47    KSC LC-39A  28.573255 -80.646895      1\n",
       "48    KSC LC-39A  28.573255 -80.646895      1\n",
       "49  CCAFS SLC-40  28.563197 -80.576820      1\n",
       "50  CCAFS SLC-40  28.563197 -80.576820      1\n",
       "51  CCAFS SLC-40  28.563197 -80.576820      0\n",
       "52  CCAFS SLC-40  28.563197 -80.576820      0\n",
       "53  CCAFS SLC-40  28.563197 -80.576820      0\n",
       "54  CCAFS SLC-40  28.563197 -80.576820      1\n",
       "55  CCAFS SLC-40  28.563197 -80.576820      0"
      ]
     },
     "execution_count": 1,
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "execute_result"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "spacex_df.tail(10)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "195cfeaf",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Next we create markers for every launch record: green for a successful landing (`class=1`)\n",
    "and red for a failed one (`class=0`). We use a `MarkerCluster` so that many overlapping markers at\n",
    "the same site are grouped together."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 1,
   "id": "919e8964",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "marker_cluster = MarkerCluster()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 1,
   "id": "d2cbdb8b",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "text/plain": [
       "   Launch Site        Lat       Long  class marker_color\n",
       "0  CCAFS LC-40  28.562302 -80.577356      0          red\n",
       "1  CCAFS LC-40  28.562302 -80.577356      0          red\n",
       "2  CCAFS LC-40  28.562302 -80.577356      0          red\n",
       "3  CCAFS LC-40  28.562302 -80.577356      0          red\n",
       "4  CCAFS LC-40  28.562302 -80.577356      0          red"
      ]
     },
     "execution_count": 1,
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "execute_result"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "spacex_df['marker_color'] = spacex_df['class'].apply(lambda x: 'green' if x == 1 else 'red')\n",
    "spacex_df.head()"
   ]
  },
